260-263	638,1062,1652,2040 - 1510,1094,1663,1342 - 1576,1608,1704,2072 - 925,1838,1125,2108	260. Branch of Papaw in flower. 263. Fruits; two of them cut through.	A leafy Papaw branch (260) with two drooping three-petalled flowers below; at the top hang the fruits (263), one halved lengthwise to show its row of large seeds, one cut across.
261	1510,1094,1663,1342	261. A stamen.	A single Papaw stamen, enlarged: a short thick stalk topped by the long anther cells under a rounded cap, with pollen grains spilling from one side.
262	1576,1608,1704,2072	262. Flower with all but the pistils taken off the receptacle.	The Papaw flower stripped to its stalk and knob-like receptacle, with the little cluster of pistils standing up at the top.
264	925,1838,1125,2108	264. A seed cut through to show the variegated albumen.	An oval Papaw seed cut through, its thick coat enclosing albumen marked all over with fine crosswise slits.
